  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>If the complex is <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi>O</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>M</mi></math> will have <math><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math> oxidation state and hence, it has already lost <math><mn>2</mn></math> electrons from <math><mi>s</mi><mo>-</mo></math> orbital. Since it has <math><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.9</mn></math> <math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo><msqrt> <mrow> <mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mrow> <mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow> <mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow> </msqrt> <mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow> </math><br /><br /><math><mn>3</mn></math> unpaired so, the configuration can either be:<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5d1c60d6-1754-44d0-a3de-0ce0e954e394-image.png\" style=\"width: 290px; height: 126px;\" /></p>",
